Fill a pressed button from the sunken step of the shade ladder

Style::getFill() fills a sunken control from step 4 of the shade
ladder, and a checked control away from the mouse takes the same
step. The getFill() of the GTK 2 engine gives the same steps.
Writer::button() painted the pressed image and the pressed ground
from step 2. A pressed or checked button of a GTK program therefore
took another ground than the same button of a Qt program.

Writer::button() now takes step 4 for the pressed image and the
pressed ground. The pressed rule of the flat and tool bar buttons
copies that box, and the pressed accent rules tint that image. The
GTK 3 sheets write the same values inline. No other rule of the
sheets changes.

The five shade tables take the new factors of the pressed rows. Each
pressed image row of the gradient table keeps the factor 0.900 of one
gradient stop.

The change sits on the branch work/gtk4-theme of the local tree, as the
eighteenth commit. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !15
on system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

